{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Whose harvest a hungry man eats</b> — he sows, and a hungry man who has no strength overpowers him and eats his harvest." "<b>and from tzinim</b> — like ולצנינים, for when the seed is not winnowed clean, its thistles multiply, and the hungry take the stalks from among the thorns." "<b>tzammim</b> — Some say: like צמאים, and the matter is repetitive, for he mentioned the hungry and the thirsty. And some say: for tzammim is the hard stone in the language of Ishmael. And R. Moses said: its meaning is virgins who possess צמות. And it is far-fetched. All toil that is with aven is like it in meaning — he says that the wicked man does not flourish; therefore a man gives birth to him, and it is as though he does not beget, but only to do toil and aven, as in: הן בעון חוללתי, for the offspring of a man are inclined to do evil, in the sense of: כי יצר לב האדם רע."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {2 "The reading וא\"ר משה is taken as ואמר ר׳ משה based on context; alternatively it could be ואומר ר׳ משה, 'and R. Moses says.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:52.758429849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}